WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning Hank; it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.000
I'm in my basement wearing a tie which can
only mean one thing: it's time for the Bank

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.480
of Nerdfighteria's semiannual report.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.370
So the Bank of Nerdfighteria is like the U.S.
federal government (or an exceptionally unhealthy

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.900
tree) and has three branches.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.390
There's the lending branch, the spending branch,
and then the giving branch.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.460
Let's start with the lending branch over at
kiva.org.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.510
More than 49,000 members of the Nerdfighter
Kiva group have loaned more than 6.3 million

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.730
dollars to entrepreneurs in the developing
world.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.620
We're the second largest group of all time
on the website; you can make loans of as little

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.450
as $25 to the entrepreneur of your choice,
and you have a 99% chance of getting paid

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.370
back, so it's like a savings account with
a -1% interest rate, which is pretty healthy

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.370
these days.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.930
There is a link in the doobly-doo below to
learn more.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.470
OK, on to the spending arm.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:46.040
So, Hank, our channels Crash Course and SciShow
are both primarily supported not by advertising,

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.630
but by voluntary subscriptions at Patreon.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.809
Basically people who value Crash Course and
SciShow and can afford to support them can

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:55.330
go to Patreon and do so so that the rest of
us can watch it for free.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:59.149
Hank, lots of people told us that this would
never work, but in fact so far, it's working

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:00.149
great.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:03.399
Both Crash Course and SciShow are now not
only fully sustainable thanks to Patreon,

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:06.380
but we're hoping to be able to expand both
of them in 2016.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.479
So, thank you.

00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:10.740
There are also cool perks if you support the
shows on Patreon; there's a link in the doobly

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.740
doo.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.740
And lastly, the giving arm.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.860
So Hank, the 9th annual Project for Awesome
starts this Friday at noon Eastern time.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.450
But the fundraising starts at midnight tonight
with the launch of Indiegogo with lots of

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:28.000
amazing perks with 100% of the proceeds going
to benefit the Foundation to Decrease World

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.970
Suck, which is the real name of our real charity,
and yes your donations are tax deductible.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.990
The Foundation to Decrease World Suck has
no overhead; everyone who works on it volunteers

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:36.990
their time.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.550
All that does it take money we raise during
the Project for Awesome and the rest of the

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.700
year and distribute it out to charities.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.150
This year during the first half of the Project
for Awesome, we're raising money for Save

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.740
the Children and the UN's High Commission
on Refugees, and during that half of the P4A

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.180
your donation will be matched.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.830
Save the Children donors have put up $350,000
of matching donations, and Hank and I are

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.939
going to match another 250,000.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:59.130
So every dollar you donate for the first half
of the Project for Awesome will be matched,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:03.740
and then in the second half, we're going to
be raising money for charities chosen by you.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:08.099
Starting on Friday, you can go to projectforawesome.com,
watch P4A videos, and vote for your favorites,

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:12.090
so that nerdfighteria kind of collectively
picks what charities we support.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.239
Also, if you have a charity that you feel
strongly about, you should make a Project

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:16.550
for Awesome video!

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.530
If you make an awesome video explaining why
a charity that you care about deserves people's

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.099
support, it could win lots of money - it happens
every year!

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:27.550
You can find lots of resources including Project
for Awesome thumbnails and stuff at projectforawesome.com;

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.650
there's a link in the doobly doo.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.379
Also, during the Project for Awesome, there
is a 48 hour livestream, starring Hank and

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:34.970
myself and many other people from the YouTube
community.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.069
During that 48 hours, you can always find
a link to the livestream at projectforawesome.com.

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:42.069
It's the one time of year when you're likely
to see my kids cover my face in sharpie.

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:45.530
Ah, I forgot to mention that before it even
starts, the Project for awesome is off to

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.160
a great start because the Foundation to Decrease
World Suck already has $80,000.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.830
Most of that is either fro Nerdcrafteria (the
nerdfighter Minecraft server) or from Vlogbrothers

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.209
ad revenue, half of which goes to sponsor
educational projects online and half of which

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:01.360
goes to the foundation, so thank you for watching
ads!

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.140
So Hank, that's the status of the Bank of
Nerdfighteria, I'm very excited for the Project

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:08.320
for Awesome, if you have any questions you
can leave them in comments I will try to answer

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.320
them.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.530
I've been pointing at my pants a lot in this
video.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.100
Hank you will also see me on Friday because
it is my year to make a P4A video.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.750
Hmm, so to even things out and bring order
to the universe, I will see you on both next

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.290
Tuesday and next Friday, then we'll return
to normal.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:20.599
DFTBA.

